# Private host entries (gitignored — this file's real counterpart is hosts.local).
#
# Copy this file to hosts.local and add entries you do NOT want published to the
# public repo. The `*.local` rule in .gitignore keeps hosts.local out of git.
#
#   cp hosts/hosts.local.example hosts/hosts.local
#
# This overlay is OPTIONAL. Most host entries are fine to publish and belong in
# the shared hosts/hosts file instead (that's what auto-provisions new devices).
# Reserve this file for things that reveal something you'd rather keep private:
#   - a routable / public-facing IP
#   - a VPN endpoint or client host
#   - anything whose name alone leaks a relationship you don't want indexed
#
# Because this file is not in git, it does NOT sync across devices on its own.
# To sync it (optional), point it at a copy in your Dropbox/Maestral folder — see
# hosts/README.md.
#
# After editing, apply with: ~/.dotfiles/hosts/install.sh

# 10.8.0.5 vpn-only-host.example
